  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `amountCents` and `createdAt` to `OrderPlaced` and kept `totalCents` and `placedAt` alongside them. ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event, so a straight rename would break them. Renames have to go through deprecation.\n\n- **Change:** the event now carries both field pairs with identical values. The old fields are marked `@deprecated` in `src/core/events.ts`, and `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated `test/app.test.ts` to expect the new fields. `npm test` passes (39 tests), and `npm run arch` reports no violations.\n- **Not touched:** the HTTP response (`GET /orders/{id}` and the 201 body) still uses `totalCents` and `placedAt`. ARCH-8 requires it to stay backward compatible, and you only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, billing-service and analytics-ingest need to move to the new names. After that, `totalCents` and `placedAt` can be removed from the event, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. Do you want me to draft a deprecation note for those teams?",
